<title>USA: CNS to repurchase up to one million shares.</title>
<headline>CNS to repurchase up to one million shares.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>CNS Inc, maker of the Breathe Right nasal strip, said Monday its board of directors authorized the company to repurchase up to one million shares of its common stock.  </p>
<p>The company said shares will be purchased from time-to-time and will be used to meet the company's obligations under its employee stock ownership plan and stock option plans, and for possible future acquisitions.</p>
<p>As of March 31, 1997, the company had a total of 19.3 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>CNS shares were down 1/8 at 9-1/8 Monday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
